\begin{center}
{\large{\textbf{ABSTRACT}}}
\end{center}


The concept of Mobile Ad Hoc Network (MANET) is nothing but collection of wireless devices without any physical infrastructure. All communications in MANET are done through the wireless media and hence do not required fixed lines or topology. MANET is temporary network as mobiles are changing their positions randomly. The communication in MANET is done by using routing protocols, whose task is to find out shortest path from source to destination, maintain route, rebuild path immediately during communication if nodes are moved. Routing is challenging task in MANET due to frequently mobile position changes in MANET.Hence this becomes interesting area of research for many researchers since from last two decades.  \\

In this dissertation, we are presenting new method for MANET routing protocol with goal of improving routing performance in terms of network load, throughput, and delay. We are presenting hybrid routing protocol by using probabilistic rebroadcast protocol technique and neighbor knowledge technique. Probabilistic rebroadcast method is based on neighbor coverage in order to reduce the routing overhead. This neighbor coverage knowledge includes additional coverage ratio and connectivity factor. The simulation study of this protocol is done by using NS2, and its performance is compared against AODV routing protocol.





