\subsection{Class Diagram}
Class diagrams identify the class structure of a system, including the properties and methods of each class. Also depicted are the various relationships that can exist between classes, such as an inheritance relationship. The Class diagram is one of the most widely used diagrams from the UML specification. Part of the popularity of Class diagrams stems from the fact that many CASE tools, such as Rational XDE, will auto-generate code in a variety of languages, these tools can synchronize models and code, reducing the workload and can also generate Class diagrams from object-oriented code.\\

